---
source: crates/nage/tests/cli.rs
expression: transcript
---
$ nage serve --help
[stdout]
Run the web server until it is stopped; it updates the database first, after a backup

Usage: nage serve [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --data-dir <DIR>  The data folder, created with its backups folder when it is missing [env: NAGE_DATA_DIR] [default: ./data]
      --bind <ADDR>     The address to listen on, an IP address and port; IPv6 in brackets [env: NAGE_BIND] [default: 127.0.0.1:8787]
      --tz <NAME>       The time zone, a name such as Europe/Berlin [env: NAGE_TZ, then TZ] [default: UTC]
      --log <FILTER>    What the log shows, a level such as info or a filter such as warn,nage_web=debug [env: NAGE_LOG] [default: info]
      --trust-proxy     Believe a reverse proxy's X-Forwarded-Proto and X-Forwarded-Host headers [env: NAGE_TRUST_PROXY=true|false] [default: off]
  -h, --help            Print help
[stderr]
[exit] 0
